        <ArticleTitle>[Palliative care and change in treatment goals for heart failure in the outpatient sector : A survey among office-based physicians in Germany on the current state of healthcare provision].</ArticleTitle>
        <Pagination>
          <MedlinePgn>45-55</MedlinePgn>
        </Pagination>
        <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00059-025-05325-x</ELocationID>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Palliative care is a crucial part of the holistic management of advanced heart failure; however, it remains unclear how palliative care is currently provided in the outpatient sector in Germany.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We conducted a survey among office-based cardiologists and general practitioners (GPs) in Germany on the current provision of palliative care for people with advanced heart failure.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">A total of 235 individuals participated in the study.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Only few office-based physicians in Germany regularly refer patients with advanced heart failure to specialized palliative care services.</AbstractText>
          <CopyrightInformation>© 2025. The Author(s).</CopyrightInformation>
        </Abstract>
